<div align=justify><font class="posted" color="#000000"><SPAN id=postcolor><FONT color=#000000><STRONG>From Star:<BR>Madonna</STRONG>, 45, still gets nervous. A Star People source says that <STRONG>at 4 p.m. on opening night, Madonna summoned her Kabbalah instructor to the L.A. Forum because she was freaking out. The pair had a 40-minute "powwow" before she regained her composure. </STRONG>The insider also says <STRONG>Madge got good luck calls from Britney Spears, Gwyneth Paltrow and Stella McCartney</STRONG>. While the aforementioned are part of her inner circle, it seems the Olsens are not. For the May 26 show, the source says, Mary-Kate and Ashley "did not get to go backstage. Madge has to approve all of the celeb meet-and-greets, and she did not approve them." Other concert-goers spotted that night: Melanie Griffith and Antonio Banderas, Reese Witherspoon, Demi Moore and Lara Flynn Boyle, who sat with Jimmy Fallon.<BR>Following her 're-Invention' tour kickoff at the Great Western Forum in Los Angeles on May 24th, <STRONG>"Madonna began feeling violently ill at her afterparty. She was vomiting from nerves or something she ate. She was up all night."</STRONG> The illness prompted the Material Girl to cancel the May 25th show.</FONT> <!--Signature--><BR></SPAN>
